    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0467" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg373"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Rodriguez.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 26th ultimo, in which, after setting forth some secondary
                    points left in doubt by the arbitration of the boundary question between
                    Nicaragua and Costa Rica, you announce that under the provisions of a treaty
                    concluded recently between the two Governments the President of the United <pb
                        facs="0468" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/> States is to be requested to appoint an
                    engineer to act as arbitrator in their settlement.</p>
                <p>The President will have much pleasure in acting upon the joint request of
                    Nicaragua and Costa Rica when made.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
